G4005.b:
⟪πεντηκοστός⟫, -ή, -όν,
[in LXX for ⁨חֲמִשִּׁים⁩, ⟦Leviticus 25:10|Le 25:10⟧, ⟦Leviticus 25:11|11⟧, ⟦2 Kings 15:23|IV Ki 15:23⟧, ⟦2 Kings 15:27|27⟧; I Mac4, II Mac 14:4; ἡ π., To 2:1, II Mac 12:32*;] ⟪fiftieth⟫. As subst., ἡ π.;
⟪(a)⟫ (sc. μερίς), at Athens, a tax of two per cent.;
⟪(b)⟫ (sc. ἡμέρα, i.e. the fiftieth day after the Passover), ⟪Pentecost⟫, the second of the three great Jewish feasts (To 2:1, II Mac 12:32; ἑορτὴ ἑβδομάδων, ⟦Deuteronomy 16:10|De 16:10⟧, al.): ⟦Acts 2:1|Ac 2:1⟧ ⟦Acts 20:16|20:16⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 16:8|I Co 16:8⟧.†

G4008.b:
⟪πέραν⟫, adv.,
[in LXX for ⁨עֵבֶר⁩ and cognate forms;] ⟪on the other side⟫, ⟪across⟫ (usually with the idea of water lying between);
⟪(a)⟫ as in the older poets, as prep. c. gen.: τ. θαλάσσης, ⟦John 6:1|Jo 6:1⟧, ⟦John 6:17|17⟧, ⟦John 6:22|22⟧, ⟦John 6:25|25⟧; τ. Ἰορδάνου, ⟦Matthew 4:15|Mt 4:15⟧(LXX), ⟦Matthew 4:25|25⟧ ⟦Matthew 19:1|19:1⟧, ⟦Mark 3:8|Mk 3:8⟧ ⟦Mark 10:1|10:1⟧, ⟦John 1:28|Jo 1:28⟧ ⟦John 3:26|3:26⟧ ⟦John 10:40|10:40⟧; τ. χειμάρρου τ. Κέδρων, ⟦John 18:1|Jo 18:1⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ τὸ π., ⟪the region beyond⟫, ⟪the other side⟫: ⟦Matthew 8:18|Mt 8:18⟧, ⟦Matthew 8:28|28⟧ ⟦Matthew 14:22|14:22⟧ ⟦Matthew 16:5|16:5⟧, ⟦Mark 4:35|Mk 4:35⟧ ⟦Mark 5:21|5:21⟧ ⟦Mark 6:45|6:45⟧ ⟦Mark 8:13|8:13⟧; τ. θαλάσσης, ⟦Mark 5:1|Mk 5:1⟧; τ. λίμνης, ⟦Luke 8:22|Lk 8:22⟧.†

G4009.b:
⟪πέρας⟫, -ατος, τό
(< πέρα, beyond), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨קֵץ⁩, ⁨קָצֶה⁩ and cognate forms;] ⟪an end⟫, ⟪limit⟫, ⟪boundary⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of space: chiefly in pl., τὰ π. τ. γῆς, ⟦Matthew 12:42|Mt 12:42⟧, ⟦Luke 11:31|Lk 11:31⟧; τ. οἰκουμένης, ⟦Romans 10:18|Ro 10:18⟧(LXX);
⟪(b)⟫ (opp. to ἀρχή) ⟪the end⟫: c. gen., ἀντιλογίας, ⟦Hebrews 6:10|He 6:10⟧.†

G4016.b:
⟪περι-βάλλω⟫,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨כּסה⁩ pi., also for ⁨לבשׁ⁩, ⁨עטה⁩, etc.;] ⟪to throw around⟫ or ⟪over⟫, ⟪put on⟫ or ⟪over⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of siege or defensive works: χάρακά σοι, ⟦Luke 19:43|Lk 19:43⟧ (WH, mg.; παρεμβ-, WH, txt.);
⟪(b)⟫ of clothing, ⟪to put on⟫, ⟪wrap about⟫, ⟪clothe with⟫: c. acc. rei, ⟦Luke 23:11|Lk 23:11⟧; c. acc. pers., ⟦Matthew 25:36|Mt 25:36⟧, ⟦Matthew 25:38|38⟧, ⟦Matthew 25:43|43⟧; c. dupl. acc. (not cl.; Bl., § 34, 4), ⟦John 19:2|Jo 19:2⟧; pf. pass., ⟪to have wrapped round⟫ one: c. acc. rei (cl.), ⟦Mark 14:51|Mk 14:51⟧ ⟦Mark 16:5|16:5⟧, ⟦Revelation 7:9|Re 7:9⟧, ⟦Revelation 7:13|13⟧ ⟦Revelation 10:1|10:1⟧ ⟦Revelation 11:3|11:3⟧ ⟦Revelation 12:1|12:1⟧ ⟦Revelation 17:4|17:4⟧ ⟦Revelation 18:16|18:16⟧ ⟦Revelation 19:13|19:13⟧; c. dat. rei, ⟦Revelation 4:4|Re 4:4⟧ (WH, txt.; seq. ἐν, WH, mg.); fut., seq. ἐν (cf. ⟦Deuteronomy 22:12|De 22:12⟧, ⟦Psalms 45:9|Ps 44 (45):9⟧, ⟦Psalms 45:13|13⟧), ⟦Revelation 3:5|Re 3:5⟧. Mid., ⟪to clothe oneself⟫, ⟪wrap round⟫ or ⟪put on oneself⟫: absol., ⟦Matthew 6:29|Mt 6:29⟧, ⟦Luke 12:27|Lk 12:27⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:18|Re 3:18⟧; c. acc. rei, ⟦Matthew 6:31|Mt 6:31⟧, ⟦Acts 12:8|Ac 12:8⟧, ⟦Revelation 19:8|Re 19:8⟧.†

G4061.b:
† ⟪περι-τομή⟫, -ῆς, ἡ
(< περιτέμνω), [in LXX: ⟦Genesis 17:13|Ge 17:13⟧, ⟦Exodus 4:25|Ex 4:25⟧, ⟦Exodus 4:26|26⟧ (⁨מוּל⁩ ni., ⁨מוּלָה⁩), ⟦Jeremiah 11:16|Je 11:16⟧*;] ⟪circumcision⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of the rite itself: ⟦John 7:22|Jo 7:22⟧, ⟦John 7:23|23⟧, ⟦Acts 7:8|Ac 7:8⟧, ⟦Romans 4:11|Ro 4:11⟧, ⟦Galatians 5:11|Ga 5:11⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:5|Phl 3:5⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of the state of circumcision: ⟦Romans 2:25|Ro 2:25-28⟧ ⟦Romans 3:1|3:1⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:19|I Co 7:19⟧, ⟦Galatians 5:6|Ga 5:6⟧ ⟦Galatians 6:15|6:15⟧, ⟦Colossians 3:11|Col 3:11⟧; ἐν π. ὤν, ⟦Romans 4:10|Ro 4:10⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ by meton., ἡ π. = οἱ περιτμηθέντες, ⟪the circumcised⟫: ⟦Romans 3:30|Ro 3:30⟧ ⟦Romans 4:9|4:9⟧, ⟦Romans 4:12|12⟧ ⟦Romans 15:8|15:8⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:7|Ga 2:7-9⟧, ⟦Ephesians 2:11|Eph 2:11⟧; οἱ ἐκ τῆς π., of Jews, ⟦Romans 4:12|Ro 4:12⟧; of Jewish Christians, ⟦Acts 11:2|Ac 11:2⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:12|Ga 2:12⟧, ⟦Titus 1:10|Tit 1:10⟧; οἱ ἐκ π. πιστοί, ⟦Acts 10:45|Ac 10:45⟧; οἱ ὄντες ἐκ π., ⟦Colossians 4:11|Col 4:11⟧. Metaph., ⟦Romans 2:29|Ro 2:29⟧, ⟦Colossians 2:11|Col 2:11⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:3|Phl 3:3⟧.†

G4088.b:
⟪πικρία⟫, -ας, ἡ
(< πικρός), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨מַר⁩, ⁨מָרָה⁩ and cognate forms;] ⟪bitterness⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of taste (Arist., ⟦Jeremiah 15:17|Je 15:17⟧, al.);
⟪(b)⟫ metaph., of temper, character, etc.: ⟦Romans 3:14|Ro 3:14⟧(LXX), ⟦Ephesians 4:31|Eph 4:31⟧; ῥίζα πικρίας, ⟦Hebrews 12:15|He 12:15⟧; χολὴ π., ⟪a malignant disposition⟫, ⟦Acts 8:23|Ac 8:23⟧.†

G4094.b:
** ⟪πίναξ⟫, -ακος, ὁ,
[in LXX: IV Mac 17:7 R*;] prop., ⟪a board⟫, ⟪plank⟫; hence, of various at wooden articles;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a tablet⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪a disc⟫, ⟪a dish⟫: ⟦Matthew 14:8|Mt 14:8⟧, ⟦Matthew 14:11|11⟧, ⟦Mark 6:25|Mk 6:25⟧, ⟦Mark 6:28|28⟧, ⟦Luke 11:39|Lk 11:39⟧.†

G4098.b:
⟪πίπτω⟫,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨נפל⁩;] ⟪to fall⟫;
⟪1.⟫ of descent, ⟪to fall⟫, ⟪fall down⟫ or ⟪from⟫: seq. ἐπί, c. acc. loc., ⟦Matthew 10:29|Mt 10:29⟧, al.; εἰς, ⟦Matthew 15:14|Mt 15:14⟧, al.; ἐς μέσῳ, c. gen., ⟦Luke 8:7|Lk 8:7⟧; παρὰ τ. ὁδόν, ⟦Matthew 13:4|Mt 13:4⟧, ⟦Mark 4:4|Mk 4:4⟧, ⟦Luke 8:5|Lk 8:5⟧; seq. ἀπό, ⟦Matthew 15:27|Mt 15:27⟧, al.; ἐκ, ⟦Mark 13:25|Mk 13:25⟧, ⟦Luke 10:18|Lk 10:18⟧, ⟦Revelation 8:10|Re 8:10⟧ ⟦Revelation 9:1|9:1⟧. Metaph.: ὁ ἥλιος, seq. ἐπί, ⟦Revelation 7:16|Re 7:16⟧; ἀχλὺς κ. σκότος, ⟦Acts 13:11|Ac 13:11⟧; ὁ κλῆρος, ⟦Acts 1:26|Ac 1:26⟧; ὑπὸ κρίσιν, ⟦James 5:12|Ja 5:12⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Of prostration,
	⟪(a)⟫ of persons, ⟪to fall prostrate⟫, ⟪prostrate oneself⟫: χαμαί, ⟦John 18:6|Jo 18:6⟧; seq. ἐπί, c. acc., ⟦Matthew 17:6|Mt 17:6⟧, ⟦Acts 9:4|Ac 9:4⟧; id. c. gen., ⟦Mark 9:20|Mk 9:20⟧; πρὸς τ. πόδας, ⟦Acts 5:10|Ac 5:10⟧, ⟦Revelation 1:17|Re 1:17⟧; πεσὼν ἐξέψυξε, ⟦Acts 5:5|Ac 5:5⟧; of supplication, homage or worship: πρὸς (παρὰ, ἐπὶ) τ. πὸδας, ⟦Mark 5:22|Mk 5:22⟧, ⟦Luke 8:41|Lk 8:41⟧, ⟦Acts 10:25|Ac 10:25⟧, al.; π. καὶ προσκυνεῖν, ⟦Revelation 5:14|Re 5:14⟧ ⟦Revelation 19:4|19:4⟧; ptcp. c. προσκυνεῖν, ⟦Matthew 2:11|Mt 2:11⟧, al.; ἐνώπιον, ⟦Revelation 4:10|Re 4:10⟧ ⟦Revelation 5:8|5:8⟧; ἐπὶ πρόσωπον, ⟦Matthew 26:39|Mt 26:39⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ of things, ⟪to fall⟫, ⟪fall down⟫: ⟦Matthew 21:44|Mt 21:44⟧, ⟦Luke 23:30|Lk 23:30⟧; of falling to ruin and destruction, ⟦Matthew 7:25|Mt 7:25⟧, ⟦Acts 15:16|Ac 15:16⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:30|He 11:30⟧; ἔπεσε (timeless aorist; M, Pr.,134), ⟦Revelation 18:2|Re 18:2⟧. Metaph.: ⟦Romans 11:11|Ro 11:11⟧; πόθεν πέπτωκας, ⟦Revelation 2:5|Re 2:5⟧; opp. to ἑστάναι, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:12|I Co 10:12⟧; to στήκειν, ⟦Romans 14:4|Ro 14:4⟧; of virtues, ⟦1 Corinthians 13:8|I Co 13:8⟧; of precepts, ⟦Luke 16:17|Lk 16:17⟧. (Cf. ἀνα-, ἀντι-, ἀπο-, ἐκ-, ἐπι-, κατα-, παρα-, περι-, προσ-, συν-πίπτω.)
